{"id":47,"text":"Sara was tired. She had worked twelve hours, and her feet hurt. When the evening bus arrived, it was almost full. She found the last empty seat and sat down with a sigh.\n\nAt the next stop, an old woman climbed on. She was carrying two heavy shopping bags and looked exhausted. Nobody stood up. Everyone was looking at their phones.\n\nSara hesitated. She was so tired, and she thought, “Someone else will give her a seat.” But no one did. The old woman held on to a pole, shaking a little as the bus moved.\n\nSara stood up. “Please take my seat,” she said.\n\n“Thank you, dear,” said the woman gratefully. She sat down, and Sara held her bags.\n\nTen minutes later, the woman said, “I have been shopping all day for my sick husband. I was feeling terrible and almost cried on the bus. You made my day better.”\n\nSara smiled. Strangely, she didn’t feel tired any more. She felt light and happy.\n\nWhen the old woman got off, she touched Sara’s hand. “Remember,” she said, “small kindnesses give us more energy than a seat ever could.”\n\nSara walked the rest of the way home with a smile.\n\nMoral: When we help others, we often help ourselves more.","tr":null,"gl":{"sara":"Sara (ism)","was":"edi","tired":"charchagan","she":"u (ayol)","had":"bor edi; -gan edi","worked":"ishladi","twelve":"o'n ikki","hours":"soatlar","and":"va","her":"uni; uning (ayol)","feet":"oyoqlar","hurt":"og'ritdi, jarohatlangan","when":"qachon; -ganda","the":"(aniq artikl)","evening":"kechqurun","bus":"avtobus","arrived":"yetib keldi","it":"u (narsa)","almost":"deyarli","full":"to'la","found":"topdi","last":"oxirgi; davom etmoq","empty":"bo'sh","seat":"o'rindiq","sat":"o'tirdi","down":"pastga","with":"bilan","a":"bir (noaniq artikl)","sigh":"uh tortish","at":"-da, -ga","next":"keyingi","stop":"to'xtatmoq","an":"bir (noaniq artikl)","old":"keksa, eski","woman":"ayol","climbed":"ko'tarildi, chiqdi","on":"ustida, -da","carrying":"ko'tarib","two":"ikki","heavy":"og'ir","shopping":"xarid","bags"